# The dogfooding entry: the repo this tool was written for, and the only corpus
# member that is itself a cpp_format *consumer* -- it imports the kit by URL and
# keeps its own cpp_format.yaml checked in.  The harness strips that wiring when
# it materializes the repo (see _strip_cpp_format_wiring); otherwise the
# scenario would test whichever binary the repo's pinned release tag points at,
# always green and never the one under test.
#
# What it adds over the Google corpora:
#
# - Plain aggregates.  googletest, abseil and re2 are class-per-file, and their
#   data members already end in an underscore, so the `member` rule is nearly a
#   no-op there.  Here half the data members live in option structs written with
#   bare names (SandboxRunnerConfig::docker_image, repo_dir, work_dir), so
#   `trailing_` actually moves them -- and moves them across the aggregate
#   initializations and designated initializers at every call site.
# - ABSL_FLAG.  A flag's name is a macro argument that absl only ever pastes
#   (FLAGS_##name) or stringizes (#name), and several of them are spelled the
#   same as a member of the config struct they are copied into.  That is what
#   the spelling audit is for, and it is the scenario's most interesting skip;
#   see the scenario file.
# - grpc and protobuf in the graph, so generated headers under bazel-out are in
#   every TU's include closure -- the aspect has to classify them as not-ours
#   and leave the generated accessors alone while renaming the hand-written
#   members around them.
# - C++23 (.bazelrc forces -std=c++23), and -Werror, which is what the tool's
#   own `-w` adjuster exists for.
#
# //...: the examples are separate Bazel workspaces with their own MODULE.bazel
# and the repo's .bazelignore already keeps //... out of them.
#
# RUN_TESTS=0: a good part of this repo's test suite wants a docker daemon.
# `build` is the assertion that matters here anyway -- a missed reference is a
# compile error, not a test failure.
REPO_KIND=git
REPO_URL=https://github.com/geligeli/game-arena.git
REPO_REV=f3e105f0d5dfc1dc6a2a6f39f336167265b8b161   # 2026-09-13
TARGET_PATTERN='//...'
RUN_TESTS=0
